      "message": "I don\u0027t think I understood your comment. Maybe you misunderstood my commit, so let me explain that. In regex ```(x)?``` is basically \"match on x **if** it exists\". Examples (I had to \u0027escape\u0027 ```$```, ```(``` and ```)```. It can be avoided with ```-E``` flag iirc):\n```\n~ $ sed \u0027s/a//\u0027 \u003c\u003c\u003c \"abc\"\nbc\n\n~ $ sed \u0027s/a\\(b\\?\\)//\u0027 \u003c\u003c\u003c \"abc\"\nc\n\n~ $ sed \u0027s/a\\(b\\?\\)//\u0027 \u003c\u003c\u003c \"ac\"\nc\n```\nThis is exactly what we used in 469881 to label AIDL Codec2 service without adding another line. This way both AIDL and HIDL services were labeled, because there was a match found for both of them. In the end, I\u0027m dropping that completely so only AIDL is labeled, because the label is redundant and no longer used by anything.",
